build(brand): applicationId com.itelegram.unofficial, app name istylegraph

- gradle.properties: APP_PACKAGE=com.itelegram.unofficial, so the app
  installs next to the official client (debug adds .beta, standalone .web).
- TMessagesProj_App/google-services.json: placeholder Firebase config for
  the new package names. It lets the build pass; FCM tokens will fail
  until you add your own Firebase project. Telegram's servers most likely
  send pushes only through Telegram's own Firebase project, so use the
  background connection for notifications.
- TMessagesProj_App/src/main/res/values/strings.xml: AppName and
  AppNameBeta override the library strings (launcher label, account
  label, notification titles).
- The contacts sync account type follows APP_PACKAGE (BuildConfig field
  and generated string), so it no longer clashes with the official app.
- BuildVars.isBetaApp() checks the ".beta" suffix instead of the
  official package name.
